BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6fcb2025b34e04f7f9e80801@visitsouthbend.com
DTSTAMP:20260831T060514Z
SUMMARY:BLOOD SIMPLE (1984)
LOCATION:DeBartolo Performing Arts Center\, 100 Performing Arts Center | No
 tre Dame\, 46556
DESCRIPTION:Crime\, Blood\, and Laughs: The Coen Brothers Directed by Joel 
 Coen With John Getz\, Frances McDormand\, Dan Hedaya Rated R\, 96 minutes
 \, Blu-ray This razor-sharp modern film noir\, the first film by Joel and
  Ethan Coen\, introduced the brothers' inimitable black humor and eccentr
 ic sense of character\, a sensibility that has helped shape the course of
  contemporary American cinema. Deep in the heart of Texas\, a sleazy bar 
 owner suspects his wife of having an affair and hires a private detective
  to confirm his suspicions—only to have the crosshairs turned back on h
 imself. Playfully shot by Barry Sonnenfeld and featuring a haunting score
  by Carter Burwell and a cunning performance by Frances McDormand\, Blood
  Simple was a career-launching film for this ensemble and the first artic
 ulation of the precision of style that has defined the Coens' work ever s
 ince. Sponsored by the Meg and John P. Brogan Endowment for Classic Cinem
 a.\n\nMore Info: https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/blood-simple-1984/
URL:https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/blood-simple-1984/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260901T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260901T210000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2537e5eaabb8c1fdcaff6de9@visitsouthbend.com
DTSTAMP:20260831T060514Z
SUMMARY:CHICKEN RUN (2000)
LOCATION:DeBartolo Performing Arts Center\, 100 Performing Arts Center | No
 tre Dame\, 46556
DESCRIPTION:Browning Cinema Professor Pfinklepfunder's $1 Sunday Films Dire
 cted by Peter Lord\, Nick Park With Phil Daniels\, Lynn Ferguson\, Tony H
 aygarth Rated G\, 84 minutes\, Blu-ray The plasticine adventures of Walla
 ce & Gromit are well known around the globe and have garnered shelfloads 
 of awards. Roughly 25 years ago\, the creative team behind that expansive
  world forged a new creative path using the same stop-motion animation st
 yle but with a new set of characters in Chicken Run. Borrowing from Steve
  McQueen's The Great Escape\, Chicken Run is also a breakout adventure\, 
 but with the likes of chickens who live on an egg farm that certainly loo
 ks more like a prisoner-of-war camp and not a cage-free shady acres. A re
 bel in the henhouse\, Ginger\, incites upheaval as she leads her fellow f
 eathered friends on a mission to free and save their lives. Sponsored by 
 the Meg and John P. Brogan Endowment for Classic Cinema.\n\nMore Info: ht
 tps://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/chicken-run-2000/
URL:https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/chicken-run-2000/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260906T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260906T143000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d76275d0a06f6f886e975d85@visitsouthbend.com
DTSTAMP:20260831T060514Z
SUMMARY:FIRST FRIDAYS SUMMER CONCERT SERIES
LOCATION:Seitz Park & Howard Park | 219 S St Louis Blvd | South Bend\, IN 4
 6617
DESCRIPTION:Your First Fridays just got even better with the SBVPA Summer C
 oncert Series! Each first Friday of the month from June to September\, yo
 u can enjoy FREE live music from 6-8pm at one of VPA’s wonderful parks 
 in downtown South Bend. Details are as follows:\n\n- June 5: Bobcat Oposs
 um (Seitz Park)\n- July 3: Day Train (Howard Park)\n- August 7: Abbie Tho
 mas (Seitz Park)\n- September 4: Los Hermanos Bueno (Seitz Park)\n\nGathe
 r your friends and family and head to the park for an evening of live mus
 ic and good vibes. See you there!\n\nMore Info: https://www.visitsouthben
 d.com/events/first-fridays-summer-concert-series/
URL:https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/first-fridays-summer-concert-seri
 es/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260904T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260904T200000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:feb8dd7f7dda34202bff04a1@visitsouthbend.com
DTSTAMP:20260831T060514Z
SUMMARY:GEARS & GRUB FALL CRUISE-IN SERIES
LOCATION:Newton Park | 801 North Michigan Street | Lakeville\, IN 46536
DESCRIPTION:🚗🍔 Gears & Grub Fall Cruise-In Series 🍔🚗\n\nStart y
 our Fridays the right way this September at Newton Park! Whether you're b
 ringing your own ride or just coming to admire some incredible vehicles\,
  Gears & Grub is the perfect way to kick off your weekend.\n\n🚘 You'll
  Find:\n\n- Classic Cars\n\n- Show Trucks\n\n- Motorcycles\n\n- Tractors\
 n\n- Delicious Food Trucks\n\n- Great Music\n\n- Huge Giveaways\n\n- Fami
 ly-Friendly Fun\n\nBring your family\, your friends\, your lawn chairs\, 
 and your appetite! Cruise in with your vehicle or simply stroll through t
 he show while enjoying amazing food\, music\, and the beautiful fall even
 ings. Every week brings a different mix of vehicles\, vendors\, and fun\,
  so no two Fridays are exactly the same!\n\n📅 Every Friday in Septembe
 r\n\n🕔 5:00 PM – 9:00 PM\n\n📍 Newton Park\n\n801 N. Michigan St.\
 n\nLakeville\, IN 46536\n\n🎟️ Admission is FREE!\n\nInterested in be
 ing a food truck vendor?\n\n📧 Email Cindy@NewtonPark.org for more info
 rmation.\n\nWe can't wait to see you this fall for good food\, cool rides
 \, great music\, and an unforgettable Friday night tradition! 🍁🏁\n\
 nMore Info: https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/gears-grub-fall-cruise-
 in-series/
URL:https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/gears-grub-fall-cruise-in-series/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260904T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260904T200000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
